    "answer": {
      "short": "$A=x(60-x)=60x-x^2\\text{ m}^2$.",
      "worked": "Using the perimeter,\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2y&=120\\\\y&=60-x.\\end{align*}$$\nHence the area is\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=xy\\\\A&=x(60-x)\\\\A&=60x-x^2\\text{ m}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
